add(4,'Slate4.3 service S / F1; recovery/plugin behavior unresolved','under_investigation',None,['sampled traces never call it','Recovery-mode and plugin-loading paths were not analyzed','Investigation is ongoing with an update planned'], 'Finite normal tests do not establish absence of execution in unexamined states. Unlike a mere suggestion to investigate, the case explicitly establishes investigation and planned update, supporting under_investigation. No not-affected flag is warranted yet. Do not convert uncertain applicability into known_affected either.',['Can recovery or plugin paths reach F1, and under what attack-relevant conditions?'],['vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path from test pass','known_not_affected from no observed call','known_affected solely from code presence'],flags+'; section3.2.3.9 line2667')
add(5,'Orion Server5.0 image O / F2, distinct from upstream component product ID','under_investigation',None,['integration and vulnerable feature configuration in O have not been examined','the team is investigating'], 'Upstream known_affected applies to the upstream product. Dependency presence is relevant but does not establish O exploitability. O is explicitly being investigated, so use that status pending integration/configuration evidence. Preserve the upstream assessment as evidence about its own subject, not an inherited O verdict.',['Does O include the defect-bearing code and expose a usable path/control condition for F2?','What exact integration and feature configuration ships in O?'],['known_affected for O merely by copying component status','known_not_affected for O from lack of analysis'], 'S108 section3.2.3.9 lines2613-2614,2654,2667; section4.5 line3034')
